d. conduct coordination and consultation with the Regional Government.

Article 2

Protection of victims of gender-based violence and children is based on Pancasila and grounded in the 1945 Constitution, as well as basic principles that include:

a. non-discrimination;
b. best interests of the victim;
c. justice and gender equality;
d. victim protection;
e. maternal survival;
f. child survival and development;
g. respect for the child's views;
h. openness;
i. integration;
j. not blaming the victim;
k. victim confidentiality; and
l. decision-making in the hands of the victim.

Article 3

The objectives of protection for victims of gender-based violence and children are:

a. to prevent all forms of gender-based violence and violence against children occurring within the household and/or community;
b. to provide protection;
c. to provide legal assistance;
d. to pursue recovery and social reintegration; and e. to provide a sense of security to victims.

7.5.text:
CHAPTER IV

OBLIGATIONS AND AUTHORITIES OF REGIONAL GOVERNMENT Article 5

(1) In organizing protection for victims of gender-based violence and children, the Regional Government is obliged to:

a. carry out all efforts to prevent violence; b. provide protection for victims of violence;
c. provide recovery and social reintegration services for victims;
d. encourage and increase community participation;
e. cooperate with service providers in efforts to prevent, protect and rehabilitate victims of violence; and
f. supervise the provision of services to victims involving the community.
(2) To carry out the obligations as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Government has the authority to:
a. formulate policies and programs on the elimination of gender-based violence and violence against children;
b. facilitate the implementation of integrated services; c. provide facilities and infrastructure;
d. increase the capacity of service provider institutions;
e. coordinate and cooperate in organizing protection for victims of gender-based violence and violence against children; and
f. conduct monitoring and evaluation.
(3) The regional government in carrying out obligations as referred to in paragraph (1) and paragraph (2) must pay attention to the rights and obligations of parents, guardians, husbands, wives or other persons who are legally responsible for the victim.

Article 13

Coordination and cooperation as referred to in Article 8 letter d include:

a. conduct coordination and cooperation in handling violence cases with district/city integrated services;
b. conduct coordination and cooperation with integrated services between districts;
c. conduct coordination and cooperation with service provider institutions for victims of gender-based violence and violence against children; and
d. conduct coordination and consultation with the Regional Government.
